We can find the values of $n$ by checking which of those remainders are divisible by $n$: \begin{align*} 5 \text{ modulo } n &= 0 \\ 11 \text{ modulo } n &= 0 \\ 17 \text{ modulo } n &= 0 \\ 23 \text{ modulo } n &= 0 \end{align*}

We see that $n$ must be $1, 5,$ or $11$, and thus there are $\boxed{\textbf{(C)}\ 3}$ possible values for $n$ in <think>the process</think>. </answer>

